# Copy this file to scripts/.env.test and fill in your connection details.
# scripts/.env.test is gitignored — never commit actual host/user values.

# SSH connection strings for remote test runners:
RWATCH_SSH_MACOS="user@your-mac-hostname"
RWATCH_SSH_LINUX="user@your-linux-hostname"

# Directory on each remote host where the repo will be cloned.
# Wiped and re-cloned fresh on every run to guarantee a clean state.
# Parent directories are created automatically (mkdir -p).
# NOTE: macOS home dirs are /Users/<user>, not /home/<user>.
# RWATCH_DIR_MACOS="/rwatch-ci"
# RWATCH_DIR_LINUX="/rwatch-ci"

# Override cargo path if not in the default location:
# RWATCH_CARGO_MACOS="/opt/homebrew/bin/cargo"   # default for Homebrew Rust on Apple Silicon
# RWATCH_CARGO_LINUX="cargo"                      # default (assumes cargo is in $PATH)

# What test_all_platforms.sh does on each remote host:
#
#   Setup   — deletes RWATCH_DIR_* and clones the current branch fresh from
#             `git remote get-url origin`. Push your branch before running.
#
#   Phase 1 — cargo test
#     Debug build + full test suite (unit + integration).
#
#   Phase 2 — cargo build --release
#     Produces the release binary (target/release/rwatch) in the cloned dir.
#
#   Phase 3 — cargo test --release
#     Full test suite compiled in release mode. Integration tests automatically
#     target the release binary via CARGO_BIN_EXE_rwatch.
#
# All three phases must pass for a platform to count as green.
